#! ia 1.0

@capability template-method
  meaning
    says "Work with template records under the IA methodology: the template-method playbook's orient, plan, act and learn cells for finding, planning, changing and checking a template. It grants no authority; the workspace's mandates decide what the participant may change."
    answers "Which procedure does an agent follow for a template?"
  composition
    playbooks [@playbook template-method]
  execution
    effects [read, local-write]

@playbook template-method
  meaning
    says "How an agent works with template records, each bounded rendering inputs and an output structure, which rendering neither publishes nor installs: orient through ia position --word template and the word's schema, plan through the owner of the word, change records only through ia preview, ia author and ia validate, and leave the account reconciled."
    answers "How does an agent work with template records?"
  subject
    subject-word template
  cognition
    orient
      primary Attention
      Attention means "Run ia position --word template at the seat the work concerns, read the template records it points at with ia read, and run ia vocabulary template --schema for the sections and fields a template carries."
      Inference means "Read the template's inputs and output structure."
      Decision means "template is a word of template-system: when the seat is not that system or a workspace that composes it, re-seat with ia position --seat floor/definition/system/template-system before going on; its steward pointer is to read, not to invoke."
      Learning means "Read the observations and improvements earlier work left on these template records before repeating it."
    plan
      primary Inference
      Attention means "Restate what the template must satisfy: the intent, the blocking rules and the mandate at the seat, and the ceiling of any provisional foundation."
      Inference means "Bound the inputs and the output structure the template renders."
      Decision means "Extend an existing template through its owner where one covers the need, and bring each consequential choice to the person with a recommendation."
      Learning means "Say how the template will be judged and what would leave it inconclusive."
    act
      primary Decision
      Attention means "Read what ia preview compiles for the template; a refusal means the plan is wrong about the record, not that the check is in the way."
      Inference means "Author the template's inputs and output; rendering it publishes and installs nothing."
      Decision means "Change template records only through ia preview template <name> <field>=<value>..., then ia author with the same form and the digest preview returned, then ia validate; use --set or --relate the same way for one field or relationship."
      Learning means "Keep each refusal with its code, fix it within the step, and preview again."
    learn
      primary Learning
      Attention means "Run ia validate and the checks that apply, report them verbatim, and say which claims they evidence and which stay unevaluated."
      Inference means "Render it with sample inputs and check the output's structure."
      Decision means "Reconcile the records that cite or depend on the template, and leave the handoff packet method-handoff-packet describes."
      Learning means "Propose what the work taught to the owners concerned, as method-improvement-lifecycle describes, or state that there is none."
